@startuml ansispire-vps-lifecycle-sequence
title Saberu VPS Takeover — Onboard → Managed → Re-Audit — TARGET (as-designed)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Operator as OP
participant "Semaphore\n(control plane)" as SEM
database "Key Store\nvps-fleet-key" as KS
participant "ansible-playbook\n(in container, uid 1001)" as ANS
participant "Target VPS\nbootstrap: root@22" as BOOT
participant "Target VPS\nmanaged: user@39222" as MGD
participant "make controller-vps-smoke" as SMOKE

== Prerequisite (one-time, per fleet) ==
OP -> SEM : inject fleet private key → Key Store
OP -> SEM : add host to vps-fleet (root@22)\nfleet public key trusted on target
note right of SEM : templates bound to env carrying\nANSIBLE_CONFIG (vault-free) + vps_task

== Phase 2/3: Onboard (takeover) ==
OP -> SEM : Run **VPS Onboard**  (strategy: free)
SEM -> KS : materialize key (transient temp file)
SEM -> ANS : exec onboard.yml\n(-e env=vps-onboard-env, --private-key)
activate ANS
ANS -> BOOT : connect root@22 (bootstrap)
ANS -> BOOT : packages, EPEL(RHEL)+fail2ban, UFW
ANS -> BOOT : create managed user + authorized_keys\n(**public_key_content** = fleet pubkey), sudo
ANS -> BOOT : install sshd drop-in → managed port,\nreload sshd  (transitional: 22 + 39222 open)
ANS -> MGD : **managed-channel validation**\n(task-level ansible_user/ansible_port,\nreuse the run's key — no mounted file)
MGD --> ANS : sudo -n true  OK
ANS -> BOOT : final lockdown sshd\n(disable root/password), close port 22
ANS -> MGD : final managed login OK
deactivate ANS
SEM --> OP : task status = success\n(tcp/22 closed, tcp/39222 open)

== Cut inventory to managed channel ==
OP -> SEM : vps-fleet → managed_user @ 39222

== Phase 3 gate: Re-Audit over managed channel ==
OP -> SEM : Run **VPS Audit**
SEM -> ANS : exec audit.yml (managed inventory)
activate ANS
ANS -> MGD : connect managed_user@39222 (sudo)
ANS -> MGD : disk / memory / failed-services / reboot (read-only)
MGD --> ANS : facts
deactivate ANS
SEM --> OP : status=success, **changed=0** (idempotent)

== Automation ==
SMOKE -> SEM : trigger VPS Audit via REST,\nassert success + changed=0 / failed=0
SEM --> SMOKE : PASS

note over BOOT, MGD
  Recovery: onboard has no auto-rollback — the managed
  validation runs BEFORE the bootstrap port is closed, so a
  failure leaves root@22 open and the host re-runnable.
end note
@enduml
